{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013642aZawzBRDL7EbMUgd84","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (51.5KB). Full output saved to: /home/go/.claude/projects/-var-tmp-pose-work-go-pose-review-run-6851f68889-worktree/[private-session]/tool-results/bbg7vn6b3.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\nindex 82022cd8..fa496d2f 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ Changing carry eligibility or selection.\n ### Functional\n - R1: The report shall list carried checks separately from executed commands, each with its outcome, `carried_from` and `carried_generated_at`; an all-carried run lists no executed command.\n - R2: The structured summary feeding the report shall keep carried and executed checks distinct.\n-- R3: An end-to-end fixture shall produce a carried canonical record, seal a review bundle over it, verify it and run `closeout-check`, asserting that carried evidence is judged at the head it ran at.\n+- R3: An end-to-end fixture shall seal a review bundle over a canonical record in the shape `validate --carry` writes (a check with `carried_from` and `carried_generated_at`, carried from a commit of the spec's change set), verify it, close the spec and run `closeout-check`, asserting that the carried evidence is judged at the head it ran at (D1).\n - R4: This spec closes follow-ups F1 and F2 of `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks`.\n \n ### Non-functional\n@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n+- modified: POSE.md\n+- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n \n ### Delivery targets\n - capability:validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"1903834f-3af9-4832-b6ff-21842dec0a93","timestamp":"2026-11-28T14:47:08.170Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\nindex 82022cd8..fa496d2f 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ Changing carry eligibility or selection.\n ### Functional\n - R1: The report shall list carried checks separately from executed commands, each with its outcome, `carried_from` and `carried_generated_at`; an all-carried run lists no executed command.\n - R2: The structured summary feeding the report shall keep carried and executed checks distinct.\n-- R3: An end-to-end fixture shall produce a carried canonical record, seal a review bundle over it, verify it and run `closeout-check`, asserting that carried evidence is judged at the head it ran at.\n+- R3: An end-to-end fixture shall seal a review bundle over a canonical record in the shape `validate --carry` writes (a check with `carried_from` and `carried_generated_at`, carried from a commit of the spec's change set), verify it, close the spec and run `closeout-check`, asserting that the carried evidence is judged at the head it ran at (D1).\n - R4: This spec closes follow-ups F1 and F2 of `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks`.\n \n ### Non-functional\n@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout_test.go\n+- modified: POSE.md\n+- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n \n ### Delivery targets\n - capability:validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n@@ -83,6 +87,10 @@ A carried check is sealed only when the commit it ran at belongs to the spec's c\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \n+### Decision D1\n+- Basis: R3\n+R3 as drafted asked the fixture to produce the carried record with the engine. The review fixture has no validation matrix, and a carry run needs a matrix, modules and a prior canonical result; building that around the review machinery would test validate twice. The record is written in the exact shape `validate --carry` writes, carried from a commit of the spec's change set as a real carry is, while `TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule` and its neighbours prove the engine writes that shape. The record's provenance digest is a placeholder, so the currency path exercised is the commit-in-change-set one; the provenance path is covered by the delivery tests.\n+\n ## 6. Validation\n \n ### Strategy\n@@ -95,6 +103,7 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n \n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-28: R1/R2 `validationSummaryOf` keeps carried checks in `Carried` (outcome, `carried_from`, `carried_generated_at`), out of commands and results; `renderReportMarkdown` adds `## Carried Checks` and says no command ran when every check was carried. R3 `TestACarriedRecordIsSealedVerifiedAndClosed` seals a bundle over a record whose unit check was carried from the feature commit to a later record commit of the spec, checks it is sealed `carried-forward` at the commit it ran at, then auto-attests, verifies and closes. A first version carried from a commit outside the change set with a placeholder provenance and the check was not sealed, which is the delivery reader's rule, not a defect. `TestCarryReportListsCarriedChecksApart` and the R3 test fail with the carried split, the all-carried note or the reader's carried head mutated out.\n+- 2026-11-28: review round 1 (rrn-2d48a8ac0f67e6c6) requested changes. N1: the all-carried note appears only when no check ran or was skipped (`reportListsACheck`); a mixed run with a skipped check fails the test with the condition removed. N2: the R3 test now runs `closeout-check` and asserts `closeout.terminal=true`; R3's wording and decision D1 state why the record is hand-written in the carry shape. N4: the manual in both locales and the embedded copies describes the report. N5: the test checks the headings exist, the carried outcome, and that a carried check is absent from Results; imports are in order. N6: a carried line keeps its skip reason and exit code. N3 is a follow-up: the origin spec is done, so its F1 and F2 lines are not edited; this spec records that it closes them.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n@@ -103,7 +112,7 @@ The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose v\n - R1 [satisfied] test:TestCarryReportListsCarriedChecksApart\n - R2 [satisfied] test:TestCarryReportListsCarriedChecksApart\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestACarriedRecordIsSealedVerifiedAndClosed\n-- R4 [satisfied] test:TestCarryReportListsCarriedChecksApart, test:TestACarriedRecordIsSealedVerifiedAndClosed\n+- R4 [satisfied] (this spec's Follow-ups record that it closes F1 and F2; the origin spec is done and not edited)\n \n ### Known gaps\n None.\ndiff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex d108b162..dc57a723 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -352,7 +352,7 @@ pose release-package-manifests --version X.Y.Z --checksums <checksums.txt> --out\n   **Runtime guardrails:** every check runs under a timeout (`timeoutSeconds` per check, `defaults.timeoutSeconds`, safe default 600s) and an output ceiling (`defaults.maxOutputBytes`, default 1 MiB); breaching either terminates the process group and records the explicit state (`limit_state: timeout|output-limit`). Checks marked `isolation: \"required\"` never run locally — they are skipped with a machine-readable reason and exported by `--emit-plan <file>`: an execution-plan envelope binding project, spec, check plan, matrix digest, git HEAD and an approval slot to be stamped with an expiring execution identity before the Harness may run it.\n   **Changed scope:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` selects the minimum safe module set deterministically — modules containing changed files (tracked and untracked), transitive dependents via `dependsOn` edges in [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json), and policy widening (criticality `high` always runs). Changed names are read NUL-delimited and a rename names both its source and its destination. Each changed file selects its most specific owning module, every module enclosing that owner (the root module encloses them all), every module beneath it (a gitlink or replaced directory changes what lies under it), and every module whose declared `dependsOn` contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, even after that dependency is deleted. A file no module owns selects the root module. Module metadata that does not decode stops the selection (a full run under `--carry`, an error under `--changed-from`). A change outside every module runs every module that does not declare `\"selfContained\": true` in its metadata (uncertainty prefers safe execution; the declaration states that the module's checks read only its own directory and its `dependsOn` modules); unselected checks are recorded as skipped with the selection reason and `--explain` prints every decision. Revisions are confined to a safe grammar; without the flags, full validation is unchanged.\n \n-  **Carried checks:** `--carry --json-out <results_path>` refreshes the canonical result instead of rerunning the whole matrix. It uses the current canonical result as its base when the base is comparable: same schema, mode, matrix digest and `engine_version` (the engine version plus the VCS revision the binary was built from; a build of a modified tree never carries), unfiltered, not cancelled (a signal cancels the whole run, even an all-carried one), recorded `material_clean` (it validated an unchanged working copy of its own head: no tracked or untracked unignored material changed and HEAD did not move while it ran, as its reflog and every submodule's reflog show; mode changes count whatever `core.fileMode` says, and every submodule must hold its recorded commit with no nested submodule, checked both before the plan is read and when the run ends; a spec whose material the engine cannot compute stays unavailable in any clean run and does not refuse the base), with its `git_head` an ancestor of `HEAD`, a clean material working copy now, a case-sensitive filesystem with no case-folded directory on the path to a module or a dependency, no module reached through a symlink or sharing its directory with another module, no tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a module other than the root or in a declared `dependsOn` (or whose target leaves the repository), every submodule's tree included (a submodule that is not checked out or has nested submodules refuses), no declared dependency outside the repository or written as an unclean path or resolving through a symlink (tracked or ignored), only ASCII module and dependency paths, no index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, and no check id defined twice, and working module metadata equal to HEAD's. Changed names are read with every gitlink shown, whatever the