{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Um7JdbRR71QMFWNbhbrgJ","type":"tool_result","content":"222:pose history-check [--strict|--tolerant]\n293:pose amend <slug> [...]            # record an append-only spec amendment\n345:- `spec-format` — inspects and migrates specifications to the modern chronological date-prefixed format (`migrate <slug>|--all [--format folder|flat] [--dry-run]`, `status`). Enforces mandatory directory envelope preservation whenever companion artifacts (`amendments.jsonl`) exist.\n406:[Omitted long matching line]\n407:[Omitted long matching line]\n411:- `history-check` — verifies every `.jsonl` under `reports/history/` is git-tracked. Without that, `recurrence-check` and `stats` diverge between machines. Strict blocks; tolerant warns.\n426:[Omitted long matching line]\n841:### Amendment history before close\n843:[Omitted long matching line]\n845:Amend and close share the per-spec lifecycle lock. The append writes baseline then change and calls Sync; failures are reported without truncating or rewriting history. A partial or malformed journal requires explicit inspection/repair. `lint-spec` warns about pending amendment findings on `in-progress` specs and rejects them on `done`; `pose close` checks the same history before transition and under lock. No history remains opt-out; no policy is adopted automatically.\n849:[Omitted long matching line]\n851:[Omitted long matching line]\n950:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"02ec5234-195f-4899-976e-e4e48be12a7e","timestamp":"2026-11-28T14:47:13.450Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"222:pose history-check [--strict|--tolerant]\n293:pose amend <slug> [...]            # record an append-only spec amendment\n345:- `spec-format` — inspects and migrates specifications to the modern chronological date-prefixed format (`migrate <slug>|--all [--format folder|flat] [--dry-run]`, `status`). Enforces mandatory directory envelope preservation whenever companion artifacts (`amendments.jsonl`) exist.\n406:[Omitted long matching line]\n407:[Omitted long matching line]\n411:- `history-check` — verifies every `.jsonl` under `reports/history/` is git-tracked. Without that, `recurrence-check` and `stats` diverge between machines. Strict blocks; tolerant warns.\n426:[Omitted long matching line]\n841:### Amendment history before close\n843:[Omitted long matching line]\n845:Amend and close share the per-spec lifecycle lock. The append writes baseline then change and calls Sync; failures are reported without truncating or rewriting history. A partial or malformed journal requires explicit inspection/repair. `lint-spec` warns about pending amendment findings on `in-progress` specs and rejects them on `done`; `pose close` checks the same history before transition and under lock. No history remains opt-out; no policy is adopted automatically.\n849:[Omitted long matching line]\n851:[Omitted long matching line]\n950:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":13,"totalLines":13},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019Um7JdbRR71QMFWNbhbrgJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
