{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sTcAiSAszDrMo6Kh2VK7v","type":"tool_result","content":"841\t### Amendment history before close\n842\t\n843\tThe first non-baseline `pose amend` on an empty history copies the valid completed atomic start baseline before recording the requested change. It uses the recorded hashes/state/relations, not edited text; the new baseline event records the current declared author/time, not past approval. Schema 1 keeps R nodes only; schema 2 requires `contract_nodes_version: 1`. An invalid or incomplete start refuses the append. No start means legacy behavior; an existing journal is never silently repaired. Explicit `--baseline` continues to snapshot the current state.\n844\t\n845\tAmend and close share the per-spec lifecycle lock. The append writes baseline then change and calls Sync; failures are reported without truncating or rewriting history. A partial or malformed journal requires explicit inspection/repair. `lint-spec` warns about pending amendment findings on `in-progress` specs and rejects them on `done`; `pose close` checks the same history before transition and under lock. No history remains opt-out; no policy is adopted automatically.\n846\t\n847\t### Terminal closeout verification\n848\t\n849\tLifecycle `done` records the transition; terminal verification reads the applicable review contract and current opted-in amendment/action/federation gates. `pose closeout-check`, `pose close --plan` and MCP `pose_closeout_state(include_plan=true)` share that verifier. A done plan exposes `lifecycle_done`, `verification` with `verification_basis` and `limitations`, and `next_action`; historical pipeline steps are `not-run`, not inferred as executed. `verify` reports the current query's verdict. `pose_closeout_state(include_plan=true)` also returns a typed `handoff` when the plan has steps left and nothing blocks it: the `pose close --apply --digest <full plan digest>` invocation as structured arguments, the arguments the performer still owes (`required_inputs`, the `--reviewer` identity when a mechanical attestation is pending), the project the caller selected (by its logical id and the digest of its root, never a path), the digests it was computed from, the authority it needs and when it stops being valid; it executes nothing and is not an approval (no handoff is returned for a plan that is terminal, blocked or on an unknown read view). Every MCP tool has a declared route class (domain-direct, cli-wrapper, read-only-planning, admitted-write, external-handoff), and `pose_suggest` and `pose_get_followups` run the CLI command in process unless `POSE_EXECUTABLE` is set or the installed binary was replaced since the server started, in which case they are spawned. Existing review cutoffs and sealed historical contracts remain applicable; a legacy exemption is disclosed without inventing an execution receipt.\n850\t\n851\tFor a done scope, `pose close --apply|--resume` is readonly: verified state returns `already-satisfied` with empty `steps_run` and `effects`, while missing required proof or invalid history returns blocked with a supported repair action. Neither outcome rewrites checkpoints, starts, amendments or lifecycle. Plain `pose close` also verifies instead of repeating the transition. An in-progress plan checks the existing amendment gate before sealing. No policy, review or historical receipt is created automatically.\n852\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e1403cc7-f294-4959-9913-06a168e0040d","timestamp":"2026-11-28T14:47:15.217Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-6851f68889/worktree/POSE.md","content":"### Amendment history before close\n\nThe first non-baseline `pose amend` on an empty history copies the valid completed atomic start baseline before recording the requested change. It uses the recorded hashes/state/relations, not edited text; the new baseline event records the current declared author/time, not past approval. Schema 1 keeps R nodes only; schema 2 requires `contract_nodes_version: 1`. An invalid or incomplete start refuses the append. No start means legacy behavior; an existing journal is never silently repaired. Explicit `--baseline` continues to snapshot the current state.\n\nAmend and close share the per-spec lifecycle lock. The append writes baseline then change and calls Sync; failures are reported without truncating or rewriting history. A partial or malformed journal requires explicit inspection/repair. `lint-spec` warns about pending amendment findings on `in-progress` specs and rejects them on `done`; `pose close` checks the same history before transition and under lock. No history remains opt-out; no policy is adopted automatically.\n\n### Terminal closeout verification\n\nLifecycle `done` records the transition; terminal verification reads the applicable review contract and current opted-in amendment/action/federation gates. `pose closeout-check`, `pose close --plan` and MCP `pose_closeout_state(include_plan=true)` share that verifier. A done plan exposes `lifecycle_done`, `verification` with `verification_basis` and `limitations`, and `next_action`; historical pipeline steps are `not-run`, not inferred as executed. `verify` reports the current query's verdict. `pose_closeout_state(include_plan=true)` also returns a typed `handoff` when the plan has steps left and nothing blocks it: the `pose close --apply --digest <full plan digest>` invocation as structured arguments, the arguments the performer still owes (`required_inputs`, the `--reviewer` identity when a mechanical attestation is pending), the project the caller selected (by its logical id and the digest of its root, never a path), the digests it was computed from, the authority it needs and when it stops being valid; it executes nothing and is not an approval (no handoff is returned for a plan that is terminal, blocked or on an unknown read view). Every MCP tool has a declared route class (domain-direct, cli-wrapper, read-only-planning, admitted-write, external-handoff), and `pose_suggest` and `pose_get_followups` run the CLI command in process unless `POSE_EXECUTABLE` is set or the installed binary was replaced since the server started, in which case they are spawned. Existing review cutoffs and sealed historical contracts remain applicable; a legacy exemption is disclosed without inventing an execution receipt.\n\nFor a done scope, `pose close --apply|--resume` is readonly: verified state returns `already-satisfied` with empty `steps_run` and `effects`, while missing required proof or invalid history returns blocked with a supported repair action. Neither outcome rewrites checkpoints, starts, amendments or lifecycle. Plain `pose close` also verifies instead of repeating the transition. An in-progress plan checks the existing amendment gate before sealing. No policy, review or historical receipt is created automatically.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":841,"totalLines":1087}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013sTcAiSAszDrMo6Kh2VK7v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
